{"availability":"available","full":"jpylephilalegal/docassemble-electronicsignaturels","name":"docassemble-electronicsignaturels","description":"Integrating Legal Server with docassemble for purposes of gathering e-signatures on documents that are then stored in Legal Server.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":9,"forks":2,"created":"2018-09-09T02:35:34Z","updated":"2019-04-11T14:06:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T16:22:58.614Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T16:22:58.614Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T16:22:58.614Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T16:22:58.614Z","stars":9,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:49.483Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a [docassemble] add-on package that demonstrates a method of integrating Legal Server with [docassemble] for the purpose of gathering electronic signatures from clients.","You will need a [docassemble] server that is accessible from the internet. Since [docassemble] is free software, you can install it on a physical machine or a virtual machine on your own premises, and then configure your firewall so that the outside world can access the machine on ports 80 and 443. There will be no out-of-pocket monthly cost for this approach.","Another approach, which most people use, is to run a [docassemble] server \"in the cloud\" using the [Docassemble Toolkit] service. Or, if you are comfortable with setting up virtual machines in the cloud, you can host it yourself in the cloud using a service like [Amazon Web Services], [Digital Ocean], or [Microsoft Azure]. The [Docassemble Toolkit] service costs about the same per month as using [Amazon Web Services] on your own."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jpylephilalegal/docassemble-electronicsignaturels/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"a883c0d9e8800296458afe9be6678a22d60d520bfc08badfa7247